# Code owners for the surfaces that grant authority (ADR-0035).
#
# The workflows decide which credentials exist and where packages and images are
# published; the zizmor policy and Dependabot config decide how the action supply chain
# is pinned and kept current; the pre-commit, gitleaks, justfile and pyproject
# configuration decide which checks run and how a release is cut; the Dockerfile decides
# what the published image contains. One approval should not be able to move a grant and
# relax the check that reports on it in the same diff, so each surface is owned.
#
# This file only requests review. It has teeth only with branch protection set to require
# code-owner review on the default branch -- if that is not enabled, this is documentation.
# Nothing here can assert the branch-protection setting, and that limit is stated rather
# than implied.

# The pipeline: the four workflows, the zizmor policy and Dependabot.
/.github/                                   @ravensorb
/.github/workflows/                         @ravensorb
/.github/zizmor.yml                         @ravensorb
/.github/dependabot.yml                     @ravensorb

# The decisions the pipeline points at.
/docs/adr/                                  @ravensorb

# The gate and release configuration: which checks run, over which files, and how a
# version is derived and a release tag is cut.
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                    @ravensorb
/.gitleaks.toml                             @ravensorb
/justfile                                   @ravensorb
/pyproject.toml                             @ravensorb
# gitleaks' inherited default allowlist skips this file by path (ADR-0037), so review is
# the only control over what lands in it.
/poetry.lock                                @ravensorb
/docker/Dockerfile                         @ravensorb

# Agent instructions. Tooling is told to "READ its entire contents and follow its
# directions exactly", these trees are excluded from the linting gates, and the agents
# that read them hold write access. That combination makes them executable surface in
# every sense that matters, so they are reviewed like it. gitleaks still scans them; they
# have no repository-side integrity record (ADR-0035 Consequences).
/AGENTS.md                                  @ravensorb
/CLAUDE.md                                  @ravensorb
/.agents/                                   @ravensorb
/.claude/                                   @ravensorb
/.github/agents/                            @ravensorb
